... 
... ### 4. Maiden / Alternate Name (for women, name changes, professional aliase
... s)
... **Goal**: Catch records under a previous or alternate name.
... 
... ```
... Query: "<MAIDEN/ALT NAME>"
... Then cross-reference: "<MAIDEN NAME> <MARRIED NAME>"
... ```
... 
... DOB, phone, family connections from earlier searches will validate it's the 
... same person.
... 
... ---
... 
... ### 5. Public Records Aggregation
... **Goal**: Pull DOB, phone, address history, relatives (free tier only).
... 
... ```
... Query: "<FIRST LAST>" <city> <state>
... Free aggregators that appear in Tavily:
...   - spokeo.com
...   - fastbackgroundcheck.com
...   - truepeoplesearch.com
...   - nationalpublicdata.com
...   - menstoppingviolence.org
... ```
... 
... Cross-reference **at least 2** aggregators before trusting the data — they s
... yndicate from each other and propagate errors.
... 
... ---
... 
... ### 6. Family Network Map
... **Goal**: Expand to siblings, parents, spouses listed in records.
... 
... For each relative found in Step 5, run Step 1 on them. Sketch a graph:
... ```
... Subject — Spouse — Spouse's family
...    |
...    Parents — Siblings — Their families
... ```
... 
... This often reveals the subject's heritage, hometown, and additional handles.
... 
... 
... ---
... 
... ### 7. Professional Verification
... **Goal**: Confirm employer + role from authoritative sources.
... 
... ```
... Query: "<FIRST LAST>" <employer> <city>
... Look for: staff directories, board minutes, school council pages,
...           conference attendee lists, public filings
... ```
... 
... These are higher trust than aggregator data.
... 
... ---
... 
... ### 8. Heritage / Genealogy (optional)
... **Goal**: Family origin, immigration story.
... 
... ```
... Query: "<SURNAME>" <suspected country/region> family
... Sources: ancestry.com, familysearch.org, geni.com
... ```
